title: v0.4.3b: editor reload and the missing pack picker
---
date: 2026-04-15
---
author: Labyricorn
---
summary: A Reload button picks up external pack changes, and a custom template function that broke negation is removed.
---
tags: interface, html
---
source_commit: c78872fc6067a5ecdb5b08d574037b535325259e
---
body:

**Reload.** The editor gained a Reload button beside the pack selector, backed by
a new `/api/reload` endpoint. It rescans the `packs/` directory and sends a
`reload-page` event to every connected runtime client, so OBS sources pick up
changes made outside the editor.

**The vanished pack picker.** Without `hidepack=true` in the URL, the pack picker
and New Pack button were missing. A custom `not` template function in the editor
and dock packages did not handle booleans correctly, so a check such as
`{{if not .HidePack}}` always evaluated to false. Go's built-in `not` already
handles both boolean negation and empty-slice checks, so the redundant override
was removed from the editor and dock packages and they now behave the same.

The lesson is a familiar one: shadowing a standard template function to cover a
corner case is more likely to break the common case than the built-in is.

This entry was written from the project's changelog.

[Commit c78872f](https://github.com/Labyricorn/TitleFlow/commit/c78872fc6067a5ecdb5b08d574037b535325259e)
